Done. Here's what was created:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Renders a `<ul>` with each item using your `ItemTemplate`, plus Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — Generic `partial class` with:
- `Items` parameter (`IReadOnlyList<TItem>`) — never mutated
- Internal `_items` copy created in `OnParametersSet`
- `OnOrderChanged` callback fires a read-only copy of the reordered list after each swap

Usage matches your example — just use `OnOrderChanged` to receive the new order:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
    {
        tasks = newOrder.ToList();
    }
}
```
